        "problem": "Given the sets $X={\u2660,\u25fb,\u2661,\u2662,\u25b3}$ and $Y={\u2660,\u25fb,\u2663,\u2661},$ find $X\u2216Y.$",
        "worked_solution": "The set  $X\u2216Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to $X$ but *not* $Y.$ Note that the elements $\u2660,\u25fb,\u2661\\in X$ are also in $Y,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X\u2216Y & =X-Y \\\\  & ={\u2660,\u25fb,\u2661,\u2662,\u25b3}-{\u2660,\u25fb,\u2663,\u2661} \\\\  & ={\u25b3,\u2662}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
